text:
alex: Quick thought — can we simplify the metering handshake for chunked/streaming requests? The sidecar + provisional-claims dance is causing latency spikes and makes backfills painful. Proposal: provisional_id emitted on first chunk, finalizer emits a single "commit_metering" event that carries attribution pointers. Keep ingest path append-only.

maya: TL;DR? how does this help backfills and dedupe?

alex: The finalizer's commit event is the single source of truth for crediting. If a chunk is lost we still only credit once when commit arrives. Backfills become: replay commit events into compact path. We avoid complex cross-service RPCs for every chunk.

soroush: I'm worried about ordering and early-visibility for quota checks. If we only credit on commit, apps might under/over-spend in interim.

alex: Good point. Suggest we keep a lightweight provisional reserve for quota checks (small token debit visible to caller) but treat it as transient and reconciled by commit. Reserve rows are TTL'd and ignored by accounting unless commit present.

jamie: How do we generate provisional_id without collisions? We already have tenant+reqid but chunked uploads sometimes re-use req ids in retries.

alex: Use deterministic fingerprint: sha256(tenant_id + request_fingerprint + chunk_index) and emit a parent_provisional_id computed from request_fingerprint. Commit references parent_provisional_id so multiple chunks map to same commit.

soroush: Example proto?

alex: ```proto
message MeteringReserve {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string provisional_parent = 2; // sha256(req_fingerprint)
  uint32 chunk_index = 3;
  int64 reserve_tokens = 4;
}

message MeteringCommit {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string provisional_parent = 2;
  int64 total_tokens = 3;
  repeated Attribution attribution = 4;
}
```

maya: That proto looks fine. Two followups: 1) dedupe during replays (commit idempotency) and 2) compact path for long-term audit.

alex: For idempotency, commit includes provisional_parent and a commit_seq (monotonic per provisional_parent). Storage layer treats (tenant_id, provisional_parent, commit_seq) as unique key. Replays will upsert but only first commit applies.

soroush: For audits, we should keep raw reserves for X days then GC once commit confirmed and compacted into a ledgers table. Compact job will materialize final accounting rows and a provenance pointer back to commit.

jamie: Ops question — how do we migrate consumers that currently expect immediate credit events per chunk? Need a compatibility mode.

alex: We can support dual-write for a rollout window: keep emitting existing per-chunk metering events alongside new reserve+commit events. Consumers can switch when ready. We'll also provide a migration script to replay commits into legacy consumer format.

ops-bot: deploy scheduled: staging metering-slimline v1 -> 2026-03-30T02:00Z (canary 10%).

maya: Nice. One more tradeoff: provisional reserves will increase storage churn and read amplification on spikes. We need aggressive TTL and possibly in-memory cache for recent provisional parents to avoid hot writes.

soroush: Agree. Suggest: provision writes to fast key-value (redis) for N mins, but we still persist an append-only reserve log for durability. GC pipeline compacts reserve log into commit tombstones.

jamie: Also need observability hooks: metric for "reserves orphaned > TTL" and "commit-lag" percentiles.

alex: Agreed. I'll draft RFC with: flow diagram, proto, migration plan, storage schema, rollout plan, metrics. Owner: alex. ETA: RFC posted by EOW.

maya: If you can add a short backfill playbook for when commits are missing (manual replay vs heuristic auto-replay) that'll help support.

alex: Will do. Thanks all :thumbsup:
